{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#2966","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#2966","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#2966\",\"parent_revision\":\"c6011366f46b61fdd2b83e1d781201052329a503b12ce8ef6ebd05465ccc35a5\",\"root_revision\":\"c6011366f46b61fdd2b83e1d781201052329a503b12ce8ef6ebd05465ccc35a5\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-18\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nDiscovered via a hypothesis property test written while reworking #2956's fix (PR #2964): rendering.heading_to_unknown_key()/unknown_key_to_heading() round trip is not idempotent for certain exotic Unicode characters that have special-case title/lower mappings.\\n\\nConcrete falsifying example: section_name = \\\"\u00b5\\\" (MICRO SIGN, U+00B5).\\n- heading_to_unknown_key(\\\"\u00b5\\\") -> \\\"\u00b5\\\".lower() -> \\\"\u00b5\\\" (unchanged) -> key = \\\"unknown__\u00b5\\\"\\n- unknown_key_to_heading(\\\"unknown__\u00b5\\\") -> \\\"\u00b5\\\".title() -> \\\"\u039c\\\" (GREEK CAPITAL LETTER MU, a DIFFERENT codepoint)\\n- Re-normalizing that rendered heading: \\\"\u039c\\\".lower() -> \\\"\u03bc\\\" (GREEK SMALL LETTER MU, yet another different codepoint from the original \\\"\u00b5\\\")\\n\\nResult: a section originally keyed \\\"unknown__\u00b5\\\" becomes \\\"unknown__\u03bc\\\" after one render+parse round trip -- the exact key-divergence bug class #2956 fixed, but triggered by a Unicode title-casing quirk (str.title() and str.lower() are not mutual inverses for this character) rather than by the section-name-normalization-path-mismatch #2956 fixed.\\n\\nImpact: narrow -- only affects section names containing MICRO SIGN or similarly-special-cased Unicode characters (a handful of characters in Unicode have this \\\"title-case maps to a different codepoint than the reverse lower-case operation\\\" property, e.g. some ligatures and precomposed forms). Real-world section names (agent/human-authored English words like \\\"Files\\\", \\\"Fact-Check\\\") are unaffected.\\n\\n**Research first**: The general fix likely means not reconstructing a display title purely by string transformation (lower/title) at all -- e.g. storing the original-cased display name alongside (or instead of) the derived snake_case key, so no lossy round trip through .title()/.lower() is ever required. That's a design decision (a stored-display-name field vs. a purely-derived one), not a cheap one-line fix, and is out of scope for #2956/#2964. Confirm scope with a fresh read of rendering.py's SECTION_HEADING design and models.Section before proposing a fix.\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer relying on this plugin**, I want to **section display-title round trip is not idempotent for exotic unicode characters (e.g. micro sign)** so that **the tool works correctly and reliably**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Agent task - auto-derived from input, found via hypothesis property test written for #2956\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-08-18\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"0421750e5bdc2a0770306271f899f3af40c64339125940c25bc12e88f5380844\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPUW8jQ\"}"}